SANNA, verbatim from the abstract of arXiv 2309.12724, published in Discrete Analysis 2025(2):

  For every nonnegative integer n let r_F(n) be the number of ways to write n as a sum of
  Fibonacci numbers, order not mattering. For positive integers p and N put
  S_F^(p)(N) = sum over n < N of r_F(n)^p. Chow, Jones and Slattery determined the order of
  growth for p = 1, 2. We prove that for all positive integers p there is a real lambda_p > 1
  with S_F^(p)(N) asymptotic in order to N^(log lambda_p / log phi). Furthermore we show that
  lambda_p^(1/p) tends to phi^(1/2) as p tends to infinity. Our proofs employ automata theory
  and a result on the generalized spectral radius due to Blondel and Nesterov.

